{
  "abstract": "Formalization of dimension-independent exponential entropy-quotient bounds for laws on finite vector spaces over F₂. For every ε > 0 a subspace of dimension at most 2^(320(1+ε)/ε) H(X) makes the quotient entropy at most (1+ε) times its independent-doubling entropy increment, which does not exceed the original increment. The development also proves logarithmic rigidity for sparse laws and finite weighted families, necessity of exponential dependence on 1/ε, two-input almost-additivity, and concentration of moderate-doubling sets on subspace cosets. Entropies are in bits. The entropic Marton input is obtained from the pinned PFR formalization through a proved translation to probability mass functions. The selected results are Theorems 1.1, 1.2 and 8.2, Proposition 9.3, and Corollaries 9.2 and 9.4 of arXiv:2610.38525v1; no optimality of the constant 320 is claimed.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Josiah Park"
    }
  ],
